6	/**
7	 * GAME_CONFIG handler — apply a game server's customization (variant + settings).
8	 *
9	 * `worker/index.ts` owns the job loop and its `handlers` map; wire this in there:
10	 *   GAME_CONFIG: gameConfigApply,
11	 *
12	 * Ownership + validation happen at enqueue time (lib/actions-game-config.ts), so
13	 * this handler trusts `Server.gameVariant` / `Server.gameConfig`.
14	 *
15	 * MVP SCOPE: actually pushing settings to a live game server (rewriting
16	 * server.properties / PalWorldSettings.ini / running RCON cvars and restarting
17	 * the service over SSH) is deferred. For now this handler is a safe no-op on real
18	 * infra: it records an "applied" marker on `Server.gameConfig` and notifies the
19	 * user. This keeps the portal flow (save → job → "applied" notification) working
20	 * end to end without touching customer VMs.
21	 *
22	 * TODO(real apply): per family, SSH to `server.ipAddress` (sshpass + rootPassword,
23	 * as worker/game-update.ts does) and:
24	 *   - minecraft: write server.properties keys, restart the service
25	 *   - rust:      set convars via RCON (or startup args) + restart
26	 *   - valheim:   rewrite launch args / adminlist, restart
27	 *   - cs2:       set cvars via RCON + relaunch for -tickrate/game_mode
28	 *   - palworld:  write PalWorldSettings.ini, restart
29	 * Gate the real path behind `!SANDBOX` and keep the marker/notify below.
30	 */
